---
layout: layouts/base.njk
tone: light
title: "Schedule and calendar"
description: "How the day runs at Palm River Academy, from Early Years to Upper Secondary: English, Maths and Science every morning, specialist and vocational classes after lunch. Plus the dates for the year."
---
{% import "macros/icons.njk" as ic %}

{% set heroPhoto = "gallery-twister-game" %}
{% set heroEyebrow = "Schedule and calendar · " + schedule.schoolYear %}
{% set heroTitle = 'How the <span class="mark">day</span> runs' %}
{% set heroText = "English, Maths and Science every morning. Cooking, technology, art and sport after lunch. Here is the shape of the week at each age, and the dates for the year." %}
{% include "partials/pagehero.njk" %}

{% set dayFrom = days.from | mins %}
{% set daySpan = (days.to | mins) - dayFrom %}
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Monday to Friday</p>
      <h2>The day at a glance</h2>
      <p class="lede">Doors open at 8:00 for every age. Core subjects first, while heads are fresh. After lunch, the classes where the English gets used.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="dayplan">
      <ul class="dayplan__key">
        <li><i class="key key--core"></i>Core lessons</li>
        <li><i class="key key--spec"></i>Specialist and vocational classes</li>
        <li><i class="key key--rest"></i>Arrival, lunch and rest</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="dayplan__axis" aria-hidden="true">
        <span></span>
        <div class="dayplan__ticks">
          {% for t in days.ticks %}<span style="--x: {{ ((t | mins) - dayFrom) / daySpan * 100 }}%">{{ t }}</span>{% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {% for r in days.rows %}
      <div class="dayplan__row dayplan__row--{{ r.tone }}">
        <a class="dayplan__who" href="{{ r.href }}"><span class="dot dot--{{ r.tone }}"></span><span>{{ r.who }}<small>{{ r.sub }}</small></span></a>
        <div class="dayplan__bar" role="img" aria-label="{{ r.say }}">
          {% for s in r.segs %}{% set a = s.from | mins %}{% set b = s.to | mins %}
          <span class="seg seg--{{ s.k }}" style="--l: {{ (a - dayFrom) / daySpan * 100 }}%; --w: {{ (b - a) / daySpan * 100 }}%" title="{{ s.from }} to {{ s.to }} · {{ s.t }}"><b>{% if s.label %}<em class="seg__long">{{ s.label }}</em>{% endif %}{% if s.short %}<em class="seg__short">{{ s.short }}</em>{% endif %}</b></span>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
      <figcaption>Snack breaks at about 10:25 and 14:05 are left off.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <ul class="daynotes">
      <li>{{ ic.icon("clock", "blue") }}<span><strong>Off sick or away?</strong> Tell us by 8:00 that morning.</span></li>
      <li>{{ ic.icon("whisk", "green") }}<span><strong>Lunch and two snacks</strong> every day, if you want them.</span></li>
      <li>{{ ic.icon("bus", "blue") }}<span><strong>The bus</strong> runs around Hội An, Vĩnh Điện and Đà Nẵng.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

{% set waveColor = "pale" %}{% include "partials/wave.njk" %}
<section class="band--pale">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Stage by stage</p>
      <h2>What the week holds</h2>
      <p class="lede">Mornings keep to the core subjects. The mix after lunch changes as children grow.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="stages mt">
      {% for s in days.stages %}
      <article class="sday sday--{{ s.tone }}" id="{{ s.key }}">
        <header class="sday__rail">
          {% photo s.photo, "sday__photo", "(min-width: 960px) 280px, 92vw" %}
          <p class="sday__ages">{{ s.ages }}</p>
          <h3>{{ s.name }}</h3>
          {% if s.groups %}<p class="sday__groups">{{ s.groups }}</p>{% endif %}
          <ul class="sday__facts">{% for f in s.facts %}<li>{{ f }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
          <a class="sday__more" href="{{ s.url | url }}">More about {{ s.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </header>
        <div class="sday__body">
          {% for z in [s.am, s.pm] %}
          <div class="sday__zone sday__zone--{{ 'am' if loop.first else 'pm' }}">
            <h4 class="sday__when">{{ ic.icon("sun" if loop.first else "palette", s.tone) }}<span>{{ z.title }}</span></h4>
            {% for it in z.items %}
            <div class="sday__item{% if it.who %} has-who{% endif %}">
              {% if it.who %}<p class="sday__who">{{ it.who }}</p>{% endif %}
              <div>
                {% if it.core %}<ul class="core">{% for c in it.core %}{% if not loop.first and it.coreJoin %}<li class="core__join">{{ it.coreJoin }}</li>{% endif %}<li>{{ c }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
                {% if it.classes %}<ul class="mix">{% for c in it.classes %}<li>{{ c }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
                {% if it.text %}<p>{{ it.text }}</p>{% endif %}
              </div>
            </div>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="table-note center">Teachers' names are left off; you will meet them on the tour. And yes, Boredom is a real class.</p>
  </div>
</section>

{% set waveColor = "white" %}{% include "partials/wave.njk" %}
<section id="calendar">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Academic calendar</p>
      <h2>Dates for {{ calendar.year }}</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="cal mt">
      {% for m in calendar.months %}
      <div class="cal__month">
        <h3>{{ m.name }}</h3>
        <ul>
          {% for e in m.events %}
          <li><time>{{ e.date }}</time>{{ e.what }}{% if e.tag %} <span class="tag tag--{{ e.tag | replace(' ', '-') }}">{{ e.tag }}</span>{% endif %}</li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="table-note table-note--gap">{{ calendar.note }}</p>
  </div>
</section>

{% set ctaTitle = "Come and watch a real Tuesday." %}
{% set ctaText = "Pick a morning and see the day in action." %}
{% set waveColor = "blue" %}{% include "partials/wave.njk" %}
{% include "partials/cta.njk" %}
